  "summary_en": "White paper by the NZ AI Researchers Association proposing a national AI strategy for Aotearoa New Zealand, based on the WEF framework. It recommends research funding, talent development, data infrastructure, Māori data sovereignty, ethical AI standards, and sector investment. It has no robotics-specific governance content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Increase public AI research funding via new centres and hubs",
   "Develop and attract domestic and international AI talent",
   "Build national data infrastructure supporting Māori data sovereignty, test environments and regulatory sandboxes",
   "Create a task force for ethical and culturally appropriate AI standards and regulations",
   "Prioritise AI adoption in strategic sectors such as primary industry, health, and climate"
